  "summary": "Across all 13 canvases and 78 diagrams, Phase 3 produces a well-connected technical reference with useful conceptual expansions. Every supplied edge has valid line endpoints, every peripheral is reachable from its central diagram, and the supplied text rectangles do not overlap. The main weakness is editorial: dense central trees, repeated detail and unreconciled point-local qualifications make the collection harder to navigate than its decomposition suggests. These are actionable Phase 3 choices; rendered connector routing, clipping and interaction behavior cannot be judged from this output.",
  "strengths": [
    "Peripherals usually expand meaningful concepts rather than reproduce file boundaries. Examples include changes/capture L2–24 separating capture provenance from mutation receipts, source/mapping L2–18 explaining evidence identity and ordering, and analysis/reuse L11–26 separating reuse decisions from checkpoint publication.",
