      "evidence": "agent-api/identity L21–24 says construction wiring does not prove projection sharing, while runtime/central L41–47 explicitly presents one shared projection supplied to both services. contexts/central L74–77 and contexts/binding L17–20 leave current-evidence comparison to unshown callers, while agent-api/central L91–93 and agent-api/records L10–15 describe the caller's fingerprint-based status calculation. generation/lifetime L19–21 leaves concrete apply/batch deduplication unspecified, while chat/isolate L13–18 describes receipts and persistence retries for the isolated-controller implementation.",
      "impact": "These are compatible local evidence scopes, but the final collection leaves readers to reconcile them. A limitation in one point can look like a collection-wide unknown even where another point supplies a bounded answer.",
      "recommendation": "Reconcile these passages during Phase 3 regeneration. Retain local evidence qualifications, but explicitly identify the related point and its scope: runtime composition supplies the sharing description; the agent API supplies context-status behavior; chat supplies the isolated-controller receipt behavior. Do not generalize that last implementation to every live canvas transport."
    },
    {
      "evidence": "chat/central L12 names AgentDiagrammingSessionService, agent-api/central L14 names generation services, generation/central L9–14 names revision issuance, diagrams/central L57–65 describes retention, and canvas/central L74–76 hands records to persistence. storage/central L17–28 supplies the next persistence boundary. Their supplied edges connect diagrams only within their own point, and these handoff labels do not identify the destination point/diagram. Likewise, changes/central L60–63 hands acceptance to the catalog covered by storage/central L69–77.",
